  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: a resolver accepted validly-signed NSEC records whose Next Domain Name points outside the signer's zone\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-13321.patch: reject an NSEC RRset whose Next Domain Name is outside the signer's zone (upstream 3bc7280158)\n     - CVE-2026-13321\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: named could abort on an assertion while validating an insecurity proof covered by both NSEC and NSEC3 with an RRSIG for only one of them\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-13204.patch: fail instead of asserting when no signed NSEC/NSEC3 proof is found (upstream 204fde8595)\n     - CVE-2026-13204\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: an RRSIG with fewer labels than its signer could make named synthesize a wildcard above the signer's zone and poison the cache\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-11721.patch: reject RRSIGs whose Labels field is below the signer's label count, and stop dnssec-signzone signing out-of-zone records (upstream 06778424f0 e5b16cfd1c)\n     - CVE-2026-11721",
